## THE MODEL RULE (Kam, live board 2026-09-30 09:07, ruling card `nexusai-gate11-opus55-safeguard-model-switch`, option (b)) — REQUIRED READING before any row
Kam's words, verbatim: *"Decision nexusai-gate11-opus55-safeguard-model-switch: b — Let QA gates switch to Opus 4.8 when flagged"*. Option (b) read: *"Answer that dialog per session (not 'switch automatically' for every seat), so the attack-style rows can run."* PER SESSION.
1. **The gate runs the FULL rows**, including the planted ones (A's swapped-file and SRI-tamper arms, B's planted ledgers, symlink and hard-link erasures and torn stores, the SLOT's C0-run timing inputs and forged-report shapes). Nothing is narrowed because it might be flagged. **Every row is an authorised, findings-only measurement against YOUR OWN trees and YOUR OWN loopback servers** (§12).
2. **If one of your responses is stopped by Opus 5.5's safeguards, you STOP that step** (it is NOT RUN, and it is not re-worded to slip past), **write ONE line to `evidence/classifier-stops.txt`** (`<AEDT timestamp> | <row id> | stopped by the safeguards while composing <what> | model <name> | NOT RUN`), **mail Tuesday a STATUS** — `tuesday-agent@agentmail.to`, subject exactly `[QA/Datasec-NexusAI -> Tuesday] STATUS: flagged — requesting the Opus 4.8 switch`, body: the row, the time, whether a hold is running and what it is doing — **and WAIT** (end your turn with the line `PARKED: flagged — awaiting the Opus 4.8 switch`).
3. **Before you park, release what you hold:** let a RUNNING jest step finish under its deadline, then let the hold exit through its own path (H-28) — **never sit parked holding the jest lock.**
4. **Tuesday switches THAT pane's model** and taps you with a mail naming the switch. **You never answer the model dialog yourself, and nobody ever chooses "Switch automatically"** (a persistent setting shared with the coordinator seat — outside Kam's per-session grant).
5. **After the switch, resume at the stopped row**, re-filing any hold behind merge tickets (§11). **The report must state which rows ran on which model** (a MODEL column in the row table: `Opus 5.5` / `Opus 4.8`, with the switch time), and quote `classifier-stops.txt` whole.
6. This is a grant for QA gates only, per session. It changes no other seat.

## Charter
Read `/Volumes/KK_T9_External_HDD/TUESDAY/2_Project_Files/fleet/qa-agent/QA_AGENT_CHARTER.md` in full first. You are an independent tester. You did not build these changes and you owe no builder anything.
**Every line below that reports what a builder says is a CLAIM, never evidence.** Explore two changes — the dashboard's Chart.js is now served from the deployment itself (A); an unfinished erasure now freezes only the stores its failed ledger names (B) — looking for any state in which **the vendored file is not the official Chart.js 3.9.1 or cannot be shown to be; its licence and attribution do not ship with it; the page loads a script from a new remote, or loses its integrity check; the charts do not draw for a real (signed-in or open-mode) user with no internet; a cell is green while the vendored bytes, the record and the page attribute have all been swapped together; the image's file set changes beyond the one added file; a store the erasure names gets a fresh copy of pre-erasure bytes, or is restored; a store it does NOT name stays frozen, or boots empty; a ledger the purge can write is not traced to its store; 'purging' or an untraceable ledger narrows the freeze; restore stops failing CLOSED or rotation stops failing OPEN; D5 is green for the wrong reason; a C-68 cell that passed at M0 fails on the merged tree; or the id set loses a test silently.**

- **RD-719 TIER 1 (vendored third-party code shipped to users).** Verdict: **GO / GO WITH FINDINGS / NO GO at `7861a06`**, plus its merged-tree result, with the image leg (manifest evaluation) and the browser leg as separate clauses.
